theory.intro:
A **network** (or **graph**) is a set of dots joined by lines. Each dot is a **vertex** and each connecting line is an **edge**. An edge may join two different vertices or loop back to the same vertex. Moving the dots or bending the lines does not change the network, provided the connections, arrows and weights stay the same.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.4,2.8);
\coordinate (D) at (0,2.8);
\draw (A) to[bend left=25] (B);
\draw (A) to[bend right=25] (B);
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw (C) -- (D);
\draw (D) -- (A);
\draw (0,3.35) circle (0.55);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[right] at (0.75,3.9) {loop};
\node at (1.7,-1.3) {multiple edges};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

facts:
A **directed** edge carries an arrowhead and may be travelled only in the direction of the arrow.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta, decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{Stealth[length=3mm]}}}, postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.5,2.4);
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (B);
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (C);
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (C);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A **weighted** edge carries a number beside it giving a cost such as a time, a fare or a distance.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (1.5,2.4);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$5$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$8$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, left] {$4$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above] at (C) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

